          "guid": "mryk92mxegokvz13",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delete from the cache + `forgetCluster` BEFORE awaiting `close()` (not after) so a concurrent `getDbByPath` for the same path opens a fresh instance rather than handing out one that's mid-close. A close/reopen race on the exact evicting cluster is still possible but vanishingly rare (evictions target clusters idle > 30s and never in-flight) and self-heals via the existing stale-`postmaster.pid` recovery — no data loss. See docs/128 §128.4.",
            "markdown": "Delete from the cache + `forgetCluster` BEFORE awaiting `close()` (not after) so a concurrent `getDbByPath` for the same path opens a fresh instance rather than handing out one that's mid-close. A close/reopen race on the exact evicting cluster is still possible but vanishingly rare (evictions target clusters idle > 30s and never in-flight) and self-heals via the existing stale-`postmaster.pid` recovery — no data loss. See docs/128 §128.4."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/db/connection.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 359,
                  "endLine": 370,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const db = databases.get(dbPath);\n  if (db === undefined) return;\n  databases.delete(dbPath);\n  forgetCluster(dbPath);\n  try {\n    await db.close();\n  } catch (err) {\n    console.error(`[db] eviction close failed for ${dbPath}:`, getErrorMessage(err));\n  }\n}\n\n/** Snapshot the live clusters, ask the planner what to close for `mode`, and"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
